From: rodriguezst <2828844+rodriguezst@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Oct 2025 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: phy-7nm: Add PLL stabilization delay for SM8150

On SM8150/SM8250 devices with dual-DSI configurations (like Xiaomi Pad 5),
the DSI PHY PLLs require additional stabilization time after lock before
their output clocks can be safely used by the display clock controller
(dispcc).

Without this delay, clocks derived from the DSI PHY PLLs may appear "stuck"
during enable, causing intermittent kernel panics during boot when the
display subsystem initializes.

The issue manifests as:
- Intermittent boot failures with "clock stuck in off state" errors
- Kernel panics during dispcc clock enable operations  
- Reliable boot only when display nodes are disabled in device tree

Hardware investigation shows that while the PLL lock completes successfully,
the PLL output needs 2-5ms additional stabilization time before downstream
clock consumers (such as dispcc BYTE/PIXEL clocks) can use it reliably.

Testing on SM8150 (Xiaomi Pad 5) with delays in different locations revealed:
- Delays in dispcc probe: ineffective (PLL not yet configured)
- Delays in clk_enable_regmap: effective but impacts all clocks
- Delays in DSI PHY PLL enable: effective and properly targeted

This adds a stabilization delay after PLL lock specifically in the 7nm PHY
driver, resolving boot reliability issues on affected dual-DSI platforms.

Signed-off-by: rodriguezst <2828844+rodriguezst@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
index c19890358b747..c19890358b747 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -578,6 +578,17 @@ static int dsi_pll_7nm_vco_prepare(struct clk_hw *hw)
 		goto error;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * SM8150/SM8250 dual-DSI: PLL output needs additional stabilization
+	 * time after lock before clocks are stable enough for consumers.
+	 * Without this delay, dispcc clocks using the PHY PLL as parent may
+	 * fail to enable with "clock stuck" errors during boot, causing
+	 * intermittent kernel panics on dual-DSI devices.
+	 * Hardware requires 2-5ms after PLL lock for output stabilization.
+	 */
+	if (pll_7nm->phy->cfg->quirks & DSI_PHY_7NM_QUIRK_PRE_V4_1)
+		usleep_range(2000, 5000);
+
 	pll_7nm->phy->pll_on = true;
 
 	/*
-- 
2.40.0

